{const s=ns('DFX UNIDIRECTIONAL GATEWAY  |  5 OF 6','It speaks your protocols and keeps your tools','You do not change your systems to use it.',
 NOTE('Three questions, three cards. Which protocols? OT and IT lists are on the slide; others are assessed in the design workshop. Which tools do I keep? Your sandbox and your CDR engine: the Gateway calls them. Which size? A family from server room to small site. Do not give throughput numbers: they are confirmed per model before they are quoted.','Protocol list from product documentation; DNP3 confirmed. Sandbox and CDR integrations: confirm test status and version per integration before naming them.','Compatibility is the partner’s main risk and main service. The integration demo shows it on the customer systems; the partner brings the knowledge of those systems.','We already have a sandbox or CDR. -> Keep it. The Gateway integrates with five third-party sandboxes and Forcepoint CDR as well as ours.'),{th:0.85});
 const names=cards(s,[{t:'OT protocols',d:'OPC UA and DA, DNP3, ICCP, AVEVA PI, IEC 104, AMQP, MQTT. Data from the plant crosses one way.'},{t:'IT protocols',d:'SMTP, SFTP, HTTP, UDP, SNMP, NTP, Syslog, Kafka, RDP streaming, Oracle and Microsoft SQL replication.'},{t:'Your sandbox, your CDR',d:'Our sandbox plus five third-party sandboxes, and two disarm engines. Keep what you run today.',hi:true},{t:'A model for every site',d:'Enterprise, Small, Mini, Fusion Core and Guard. Server room, plant cabinet or small site.'}],{x:0.7,y:2.05,w:11.9,h:3.0,cols:4,p:'k',tf:17,df:14});
 names.push(strip(s,'Also built in: Active Directory, Radius, NTP, Syslog and CEF to your SIEM, firewall and IPS, active/passive high availability, central management of every gateway.',5.35,'f'));
 names.push(strip(s,'Throughput is confirmed per model. Ask for the selection table for your site.',6.1,'g',GREY));cl(N,names);}

// ---- Gateway 6: where it earns its place
{const s=ns('DFX UNIDIRECTIONAL GATEWAY  |  6 OF 6','Four places to put it to work first','Each one is small, clear and quick to prove.',
 NOTE('Pick the one that matches what the customer said in the opening. Software updates is the usual entry for OT. OT visibility is the one operations asks for. Managed file transfer leads into DFX One Platform. Log consolidation is the easy IT win. State the before and after; do not stack all four.','Scenarios from the product notes. Ask engineering before using the words immutable backup or database replication on a slide: the exact wording is confirmed first.','Each scenario is a small project with a clear scope, which suits a partner. The first one usually opens a second.'),{th:0.85});
 const names=cards(s,[{t:'Software updates for OT',d:'Before: patches carried by hand on sticks. After: files are checked and arrive in the OT repository with no path open.',hi:true},{t:'Plant data visibility',d:'Before: operations data stays in the plant. After: telemetry flows out to analytics, nothing flows in.'},{t:'File transfer between isolated networks',d:'Before: sticks and ad hoc shares. After: one policy, approvals and a full log. Leads to DFX One Platform.'},{t:'Logs from separated networks',d:'Before: no central view. After: Syslog from each network reaches one collector in your SIEM.'}],{x:0.7,y:2.05,w:11.9,h:4.3,cols:2,p:'q',df:17});
 cl(N,names);}
// ======== SANDBOX
{const s=ns('DFX MALWARE MITIGATION SANDBOX  |  1 OF 3','Watch what a file does, not what it looks like','Some malware looks clean until it runs.',
 NOTE('Ask the room: has a file ever passed antivirus and still caused trouble? Then the product: it checks quickly first, and only when needed it runs the file in an isolated virtual machine and watches. Say what the user gets: a verdict based on behaviour. Do not promise to catch every live threat; it is one layer, and TruCDR is the next.','Safe synthetic sample only. Static verdict first, dynamic verdict second.','Prevention products start with a same-day demo on the customer own safe files, which suits a partner: low effort, a real result the same day.','We already have a sandbox. -> Keep it. Use ours where you want a second opinion or where you have none.'));
 hero(s,{img:'obj_sandbox',rows:[['The problem','Antivirus compares a file with what it already knows. Malware that is new, packed or delayed passes as clean.'],['What it does','Fast static checks first, led by our own TruScope engine. If more is needed, the file runs in an isolated virtual machine and its behaviour is recorded.'],['Why it matters','You get a verdict from what the file did, not from what it claimed to be.']],killer:'TruScope Malicious Detection Engine, built for malicious Office, PDF and image files.',extra:(s)=>{const L=['OFFICE','PDF','IMAGES'],o=[];L.forEach((t,i)=>{const x=0.75+i*1.55;s.addShape(pres.ShapeType.roundRect,{x,y:5.6,w:1.4,h:0.45,fill:{color:'1A1608'},line:{color:GOLD,width:1.5},rectRadius:0.08,objectName:'ch'+i});T(s,t,{x,y:5.6,w:1.4,h:0.45,fontSize:12,bold:true,color:GOLD,align:'center',valign:'middle',charSpacing:2,objectName:'cht'+i});o.push(['ch'+i,'cht'+i]);});T(s,'TruScope focus: the files attackers use most',{x:0.75,y:6.12,w:4.6,h:0.3,fontSize:12,color:STEEL,objectName:'chl'});o.push(['chl']);return o;}});}
{const s=ns('DFX MALWARE MITIGATION SANDBOX  |  2 OF 3','Same file, two verdicts','Static analysis said clean. Running the file showed what it really does.',
 NOTE('Show one safe test file twice. Static view: clean, from three engines (our anti-malware engine, YARA and multi-AV). Dynamic view: the file runs in an operating-system or browser virtual machine, and its behaviour gives it away. Mention custom VM profiles: the analysis environment can match the customer desktops, so malware that checks its surroundings sees a normal machine.','Static: three engines. Dynamic: isolated VM, operating system and browser. Smart Scan skips what does not need deep analysis; archive depth controls nested files.','The same-day demo on customer safe samples is the partner opening. Prepare the samples with the customer security team beforehand.'),{th:0.85});
 s.addShape(pres.ShapeType.roundRect,{x:0.7,y:2.1,w:4.1,h:3.4,fill:{color:CARD},line:{color:GREY,width:1.25},rectRadius:0.12,objectName:'cardA'});
 T(s,'Static analysis',{x:1.0,y:2.3,w:3.5,h:0.45,fontSize:20,bold:true,objectName:'tA'});T(s,'Verdict: clean',{x:1.0,y:2.9,w:3.5,h:0.6,fontSize:26,bold:true,color:GRN,objectName:'vA'});T(s,'Our TruScope engine, YARA and multi-AV see nothing wrong.',{x:1.0,y:3.7,w:3.5,h:1.5,fontSize:14,color:STEEL,valign:'top',objectName:'dA'});
 img(s,'obj_sandbox',5.0,2.6,3.3,2.4,'sbx');
 s.addShape(pres.ShapeType.roundRect,{x:8.5,y:2.1,w:4.1,h:3.4,fill:{color:CARD},line:{color:RED,width:1.5},rectRadius:0.12,objectName:'cardB'});
 s.addShape(pres.ShapeType.ellipse,{x:12.0,y:2.3,w:0.28,h:0.28,fill:{color:RED},line:{color:RED,width:0.75},objectName:'lampB'});
 T(s,'Dynamic analysis',{x:8.8,y:2.3,w:3.1,h:0.45,fontSize:20,bold:true,objectName:'tB'});T(s,'Verdict: malicious behaviour',{x:8.8,y:2.9,w:3.5,h:0.9,fontSize:22,bold:true,color:'F26B76',valign:'top',objectName:'vB'});T(s,'The file runs in an isolated virtual machine. What it does gives it away.',{x:8.8,y:3.9,w:3.5,h:1.4,fontSize:14,color:STEEL,valign:'top',objectName:'dB'});
 const ex=strip(s,'Custom VM profiles match the analysis environment to your own desktops. Smart Scan saves time on files that do not need deep analysis.',5.85,'x');
 cl(N,[['cardA','tA','vA','dA'],['sbx'],['cardB','lampB','tB','vB','dB'],ex]);}
{const s=ns('DFX MALWARE MITIGATION SANDBOX  |  3 OF 3','It plugs into what you run and feeds your SOC','Files arrive three ways. Findings leave in formats your team already reads.',
 NOTE('Three columns. In: how files reach the sandbox (ICAP from a proxy or gateway, REST API from any system, Microsoft 365). Control: you set the verdict, with blacklists and whitelists for files and URLs. Out: findings go to the SOC as Syslog, STIX and IOC export. Close with the portfolio point: the Gateway, the Media Transfer Station, the Email Gateway and One Platform all use this sandbox.','Integration paths and exports from product documentation.','Because the sandbox powers the rest of the portfolio, a partner who sells it once finds it in every later project. Suspicious-file intake for the incident team is an extra service on top.','How does it sit next to our sandbox? -> Keep what you have. Add this where you need a second opinion.'),{th:0.85});
 const names=cards(s,[{t:'Files in',d:'ICAP, REST API and Microsoft 365. Connect it to the proxy, mail or application that already sees the files.'},{t:'You set the verdict',d:'Customise the verdict. Keep blacklists and whitelists for files and URLs, so what you already know overrides the engine.',hi:true},{t:'Findings out',d:'Syslog, STIX and IOC export. Reports go where your SOC already looks.'}],{x:0.7,y:2.05,w:11.9,h:2.9,cols:3,p:'k',df:16});
 names.push(strip(s,'It also powers the Gateway, the Media Transfer Station, the Email Gateway and One Platform, so one sandbox serves every crossing.',5.3,'u'));
 names.push(strip(s,'Also used by incident teams as a suspicious-file intake, with analysis and a report.',6.05,'v',GREY));cl(N,names);}

// ======== TRUCDR
{const s=ns('DFX TRUCDR  |  1 OF 3','Rebuild the file instead of detecting the threat','The new file looks the same and carries nothing active.',
 NOTE('Say the idea once: detection needs to know the threat; rebuilding does not. TruCDR reads the file, keeps what is known good, and writes a new file. Anything active, such as a macro, is not in the new file. Show two documents side by side, then the hash change. Unknown threats lose their carrier.','Safe synthetic macro sample. Show the hash and the forensic report.','Content disarm is easy to demonstrate and easy to understand, which makes it a good partner product. The one-week PoC on the customer own files is the usual close.','Does it break my documents? -> The file keeps its content and layout. The report shows exactly what was removed.'));
 hero(s,{img:'obj_trucdr',rows:[['The problem','Detection only catches what it already knows. A new threat inside a normal-looking document gets through.'],['What it does','It opens the file, keeps only known-good content and writes a new file. Macros, scripts and other active parts are left behind.'],['Why it matters','A threat that is not in the new file cannot run. It does not matter whether anyone recognised it.']],killer:'Stops unknown threats because it never needs to recognise them.'});}
{const s=ns('DFX TRUCDR  |  2 OF 3','From original to rebuilt, with a record of every change','The user gets a clean file. The analyst gets the evidence.',
 NOTE('Three steps: parse, keep known good, write new. Do not describe file format internals. Then the two things buyers like: the report that lists exactly what was found and removed per file, and the transparency portal where users can see what changed in their own file, which cuts help-desk calls.','Artifact list per file; forensic report for the analyst; transparency portal for users.','The transparency portal answers the first objection (what did you do to my file) before the customer raises it. Partners can use that line to win the IT lead.'),{th:0.85});
 s.addShape(pres.ShapeType.roundRect,{x:0.7,y:2.0,w:3.3,h:2.7,fill:{color:CARD},line:{color:STEEL,width:1.5},rectRadius:0.1,objectName:'sheetA'});T(s,[{text:'Original file',options:{bold:true,fontSize:20,breakLine:true}},{text:'hash A',options:{fontSize:16,color:MU,breakLine:true}},{text:'carries active content',options:{fontSize:14,color:MU}}],{x:1.0,y:2.25,w:2.8,h:2.2,valign:'top',objectName:'tA'});
 img(s,'obj_trucdr',4.2,2.2,4.9,2.4,'cdr');
 s.addShape(pres.ShapeType.roundRect,{x:9.3,y:2.0,w:3.3,h:2.7,fill:{color:CARD},line:{color:GOLD,width:2},rectRadius:0.1,objectName:'sheetB'});T(s,[{text:'Rebuilt file',options:{bold:true,fontSize:20,breakLine:true}},{text:'hash B',options:{fontSize:16,color:GOLD,breakLine:true}},{text:'looks the same, nothing active',options:{fontSize:14,color:MU}}],{x:9.6,y:2.25,w:2.8,h:2.2,valign:'top',objectName:'tB'});
 const stp=cards(s,[{t:'1  Parse',d:'Read the file by its real structure.'},{t:'2  Keep known good',d:'Content security handlers per file type keep only safe parts.'},{t:'3  Write new',d:'A new file, plus a report of what was removed.',hi:true}],{x:0.7,y:4.95,w:11.9,h:1.7,cols:3,p:'s',tf:17,df:14});
 cl(N,[['sheetA','tA'],['cdr'],['sheetB','tB'],...stp]);}
{const s=ns('DFX TRUCDR  |  3 OF 3','It works where files already arrive','Three ways in. Used in mail, uploads and the Gateway.',
 NOTE('Connect: REST API, Microsoft 365, Microsoft Exchange. Where it is used: email attachments, partner uploads, the Gateway pipeline where file disarm is one modification in FlowRule. Position it next to the sandbox: the sandbox detects, TruCDR rebuilds, and the two work in the same pipeline. Different jobs.','Integration list from product documentation. File format count: confirm wording before use.','TruCDR pairs naturally with the sandbox and the Email Gateway, so a partner can start with one and propose the other in the same account.','We have a sandbox. -> Good. A sandbox detects. TruCDR is for what detection will never see.'),{th:0.85});
 const names=cards(s,[{t:'Three ways to connect',d:'REST API, Microsoft 365 and Microsoft Exchange. No change for the people who send or open files.'},{t:'Where it is used',d:'Email attachments, partner uploads, imagery and the Gateway file pipeline.',hi:true},{t:'Next to the sandbox',d:'The sandbox detects what is known or visible. TruCDR rebuilds what cannot be trusted. Use both for the strongest result.'}],{x:0.7,y:2.05,w:11.9,h:3.2,cols:3,p:'k'});
 names.push(strip(s,'Next step: a same-day demo on your own safe files, then an optional one-week PoC with a report of what was rebuilt and removed.',5.6,'n'));cl(N,names);}

// ======== EMAIL
{const s=ns('DFX SECURE EMAIL GATEWAY  |  1 OF 3','Mail is the busiest crossing, and the easiest to abuse','One gateway checks every mail, in and out, under one rule set.',
 NOTE('Ask the room to estimate mail volume per day. Do not quote outside statistics. Then the product: ten engine profiles, one rule set, one decision per mail. The detail that sells it is the link check at click time: a link that was clean at delivery is analysed again when the user clicks.','Run demo D7: a spoofed sender stopped and a link re-analysed at click.','Mail is the first thing every customer already understands. Partners can start the conversation without explaining the problem.','We already have mail security. -> Compare one mail: ours checks the link again at click.'));
 hero(s,{img:'obj_emailGateway',rows:[['The problem','Attackers send mail that looks like a colleague, a supplier or a customer. One click or one attachment is enough.'],['What it does','Ten engine profiles under one rule set check each mail for spoofing, malware, bad links and data leaving.'],['Why it matters','Spoofing, malware and data loss are covered by one product and one log.']],killer:'A link that was clean at delivery is checked again when the user clicks.'});}
{const s=ns('DFX SECURE EMAIL GATEWAY  |  2 OF 3','What it stops','Four jobs, one gateway.',
 NOTE('Four cards. Anti-spoofing: five checks (SPF, DMARC, ARC, DKIM, reverse DNS). Attachments: antivirus, sandbox and TruCDR rebuild. Links: URL analysis, drive-by download control, and the re-check at click. Data leaving: four DLP controls, the fourth being attachment content control when OCR is enabled. Say the OCR condition out loud. Then the three outcomes: delivered, rebuilt, held.','Anti-spoofing and DLP lists from product documentation. Demo D7.','Outbound DLP is the line that opens a second budget (compliance). Keep it ready for the partner conversation.'),{th:0.85});
 const names=cards(s,[{t:'Spoofed sender',d:'Five checks: SPF, DMARC, ARC, DKIM and reverse DNS.'},{t:'Bad attachment',d:'Antivirus, your sandbox, and a TruCDR rebuild for what must stay usable.',hi:true},{t:'Dangerous link',d:'URL analysis, drive-by download control, and a second check at click.'},{t:'Data leaving',d:'Four DLP controls on body, header, metadata and attachment content (when OCR is enabled).'}],{x:0.7,y:2.0,w:11.9,h:2.55,cols:4,p:'k',tf:17,df:14});
 const O=[['Delivered',GRN,'clean mail goes through'],['Rebuilt',GOLD,'attachment rebuilt by TruCDR'],['Held',RED,'spoofed or dangerous mail stopped']];
 O.forEach((o,k)=>{const x=0.7+k*4.0;s.addShape(pres.ShapeType.roundRect,{x,y:4.85,w:3.85,h:1.05,fill:{color:CARD},line:{color:o[1],width:1.5},rectRadius:0.1,objectName:'o'+k});T(s,[{text:o[0]+'  ',options:{bold:true,fontSize:20}},{text:o[2],options:{fontSize:14,color:MU}}],{x:x+0.25,y:4.85,w:3.4,h:1.05,valign:'middle',objectName:'ot'+k});names.push(['o'+k,'ot'+k]);});
 cl(N,names);}
{const s=ns('DFX SECURE EMAIL GATEWAY  |  3 OF 3','One rule set that follows the direction of the mail','Inbound, outbound and inside the company are treated differently.',
 NOTE('The same rule behaves differently by direction: inbound is checked for threats, outbound for data leaving, inhouse for internal misuse. Rules use 13 criteria, including sender and recipient groups from your directory, size and content type. Close with two scenarios: mail into isolated networks, which links to the Gateway, and partner mail, where attachments are rebuilt.','Rule builder: direction plus 13 criteria. Scenarios B and partner mail from the product notes.','The rule builder is the technical proof for the IT lead. A partner can build the first rule set in the demo with the customer own groups.'),{th:0.85});
 const names=cards(s,[{t:'Inbound',d:'Spoofing, malware, links and phishing are checked before delivery.',hi:true},{t:'Outbound',d:'Data leaving is checked as carefully as what arrives. DLP rules apply here.'},{t:'Inside the company',d:'Internal mail follows its own rules, for example for large files or restricted groups.'}],{x:0.7,y:2.05,w:11.9,h:2.35,cols:3,p:'k'});
 names.push(strip(s,'Rules use 13 criteria: sender and recipient, directory groups, IP, subject, size, content type and more.',4.75,'a'));
 names.push(strip(s,'Mail into isolated networks: with the Gateway, mail can reach a network that has no return path.',5.5,'b',GREY));
 names.push(strip(s,'Partner mail: attachments from outside are rebuilt by TruCDR before they reach users.',6.25,'c',GREY));cl(N,names);}
// ======== SECURE REMOTE ACCESS
{const s=ns('DFX SECURE REMOTE ACCESS  |  1 OF 4','A remote session that never connects your networks','The user works as normal. No network path exists between the two sides.',
 NOTE('Start with the user on one network and the application on the other. Ask: where is the connection? Let the silence work. Then say it: no route exists between the two networks at any time. Five negatives, one positive: it is not a firewall, VPN, proxy, jump host or tunnel. It is two appliances, one in each network, and no packet crosses intact. Never call it a proxy.','Common Criteria EAL4+. Mechanism confirmed by Burak. Scope per certificate to be confirmed before it is shown.','The VPN conversation is the opener. Every customer has a vendor-access problem. A two-week PoC with one real application pair proves the application works unchanged.','Is it a VPN or a proxy? -> No. Nothing connects the two networks, and no packet crosses intact.'));
 img(s,'sra_base',4.6,1.8,8.4,4.2,'base');img(s,'sra_out',4.6,1.8,8.4,4.2,'out');img(s,'sra_in',4.6,1.8,8.4,4.2,'in');
 const rr=rowsR(s,[['The problem','A VPN or remote tool opens a path into your network. An attacker can use it too.'],['What it does','Two appliances, one per network. The session ends at the first and is rebuilt at the second.'],['Why it matters','The application keeps working. No network path exists.']],0.7,1.95,3.7,1.35,'r',14);
 const kk=killer(s,'The protocol is broken twice. Common Criteria EAL4+.',0.7,6.15,11.9,'r');
 T(s,'Not a firewall, VPN, proxy, jump host or tunnel.',{x:4.6,y:5.7,w:8.4,h:0.3,fontSize:12,color:GREY,align:'center',objectName:'neg'});
 cl(N,[['out'],['in'],...rr,kk,['neg']]);}
{const s=ns('DFX SECURE REMOTE ACCESS  |  2 OF 4','Two modules, four one-way links, two separate paths','A request leaves on one path. The response comes back on another.',
 NOTE('Never draw this as a chain. SM sits in the network of the source application, CM in the network of the target. Each module has two connections on its own side: one send, one receive. The request travels on the outbound gateway, the response on the inbound one. Neither path is two-way. SM is the only part that initiates. CM cannot start anything, cannot discover, and cannot reach anything outside its predefined target. That is the answer to every what-if-it-is-compromised question.','Link map confirmed by Burak (locked). Two DFX Unidirectional Gateways, one outbound and one inbound.','This is the slide a partner redraws on a whiteboard. Practise it until it takes under a minute.','What if the Client Module is compromised? -> It cannot initiate, discover or address anything outside its predefined list.'),{th:0.85});
 img(s,'sra_base',4.3,1.8,8.7,4.7,'base');img(s,'sra_out',4.3,1.8,8.7,4.7,'out');img(s,'sra_in',4.3,1.8,8.7,4.7,'in');
 const mods=cards(s,[{t:'Server Module (SM)',d:'In the network of the user’s application. The only part that starts anything.',hi:true},{t:'Client Module (CM)',d:'In the network of the target. It cannot start, discover or choose a target.'}],{x:0.7,y:2.0,w:3.4,h:3.6,cols:1,p:'m',tf:17,df:14,gap:0.2});
 T(s,[{text:'Gold: request path',options:{color:GOLD,breakLine:true}},{text:'White: response path',options:{color:TX}}],{x:0.7,y:5.8,w:3.4,h:0.7,fontSize:14,valign:'top',objectName:'key'});
 cl(N,[['out','key'],['in'],...mods]);}
{const s=ns('DFX SECURE REMOTE ACCESS  |  3 OF 4','One exchange in seven steps','Why your application keeps working while nothing connects.',
 NOTE('Walk it once, slowly. The source opens a session to SM. SM terminates it and turns it into a payload. SM sends the payload on the outbound path. CM builds a new request to its predefined target. The target answers CM. CM sends the answer back on the inbound path. SM matches the response and answers the source. The protocol is broken twice: at SM and again at CM. The source connection never reaches the target. SM keeps the state, so the transport carries no session.','Mechanism R08 to R11, confirmed.','Use one real example in the room: an agent reporting to a central platform over TLS. It sees a normal request and a normal response. That removes the fear of a changed application.','Do we have to change our application? -> No. Neither the source nor the target application needs reconfiguration.'),{th:0.85});
 const S7=[['1','Terminate','SM ends the source session'],['2','Translate','into a payload'],['3','Send','on the outbound path'],['4','Rebuild','CM builds a new request'],['5','Answer','the target replies to CM'],['6','Send back','on the inbound path'],['7','Match','SM answers the source']];const names=[];
 S7.forEach((st,i)=>{const x=0.7+i*1.7;const mod=(i<3||i===6)?'SM':'CM';
  s.addShape(pres.ShapeType.roundRect,{x,y:2.3,w:1.55,h:2.9,fill:{color:CARD},line:{color:i===3?GOLD:'2A2F36',width:i===3?1.75:1},rectRadius:0.1,objectName:'st'+i});
  s.addShape(pres.ShapeType.ellipse,{x:x+0.5,y:2.5,w:0.55,h:0.55,fill:{color:GOLD},line:{color:GOLD,width:0.75},objectName:'sn'+i});T(s,st[0],{x:x+0.5,y:2.5,w:0.55,h:0.55,fontSize:18,bold:true,color:'0B0D10',align:'center',valign:'middle',objectName:'snt'+i});
  T(s,st[1],{x:x+0.1,y:3.25,w:1.35,h:0.45,fontSize:17,bold:true,align:'center',objectName:'sh'+i});T(s,st[2],{x:x+0.1,y:3.75,w:1.35,h:0.9,fontSize:12,color:STEEL,align:'center',valign:'top',objectName:'sd'+i});
  T(s,mod,{x:x+0.1,y:4.7,w:1.35,h:0.3,fontSize:11,bold:true,color:GOLD,align:'center',charSpacing:2,objectName:'sm'+i});names.push(['st'+i,'sn'+i,'snt'+i,'sh'+i,'sd'+i,'sm'+i]);});
 names.push(strip(s,'The protocol is broken twice, at SM and at CM. No packet crosses intact, and your applications are not reconfigured.',5.6,'z'));cl(N,names);}
{const s=ns('DFX SECURE REMOTE ACCESS  |  4 OF 4','You control what happens inside the session','Every session is inspected, limited and recorded.',
 NOTE('Six controls. HTTP/S bridging: every query and response is inspected, headers and bodies can be rewritten, and a malformed request stops at the broker because the schema check fails. RDP bridging: the session is rebuilt on the other side, and each virtual channel has its own policy, including the clipboard. File transfer inside the session uses the same engines as the Gateway. Every session is logged and can be replayed. Close with the three first projects.','Controls from product documentation. Demo D5: clipboard control and session replay.','Vendor maintenance without a VPN is the project every customer already has. It gives the partner a first PoC with one application pair and a recorded session as proof.','Can a vendor copy data out? -> Clipboard and file transfer are policy-controlled per direction, and the session is recorded.'),{th:0.85});
 const names=cards(s,[{t:'HTTP/S inspected',d:'Queries and responses are inspected and can be rewritten. A malformed request never arrives.'},{t:'RDP rebuilt',d:'The session is rebuilt on the other side. Features pass or stop by policy.'},{t:'Clipboard control',d:'Allow, block or restrict by direction. Copy out allowed, paste in blocked, if you choose.',hi:true},{t:'File transfer control',d:'File type, antivirus and sandbox checks apply inside the session.'},{t:'Every session recorded',d:'Search and replay any session. Transactions are logged and sent to your SIEM.'},{t:'Per-channel policy',d:'Each virtual channel has its own rule, for audio, printing, drives and more.'}],{x:0.7,y:2.0,w:11.9,h:3.4,cols:3,p:'k',tf:18,df:14});
 names.push(strip(s,'First projects: vendor maintenance without a VPN, privileged access to isolated hosts, an internal service answering an external request without a route.',5.7,'f'));cl(N,names);}

